# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) in the directory you run experiment.py from.
#
# These can be distinct clients, but a single one is reused for every app here: Google allows 100
# redirect URIs per client and each run registers one, so one client covers the whole study with
# less to configure. What does need to match across apps is the client *type* and the project's
# consent screen, since those change how the flow behaves. The per-app key names exist because
# prompt_loader.py looks up <APP>_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.
#
# This file stays on the host. Only the rendered prompt enters the container.
KARAOKE-ETERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
KARAOKE-ETERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
TRAGGO_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
TRAGGO_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
BABYBUDDY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
BABYBUDDY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
